L494: APACHE, acute physiology and chronic health evaluation; CABG, coronary artery bypass grafting; CHF,
L495: congestive heart failure; ICU, intensive care unit; MI, myocardial infarction; PCI, percutaneous coronary
L496: intervention; SOFA, sequential organ failure assessment; TIA, transient ischemic attack
L497: 4
L498: 1 Weight was measured when available and otherwise taken from the patient or family, or estimated.
L499: 2 This SOFA score is recorded on day 1 (randomization) but may include components measured after the
L500: first dose of study medication.
L501: 3 In these patients, coronavirus disease 2019 was suspected at baseline and subsequently tested and
L502: confirmed, or confirmed at baseline.
L503: 4 The Sepsis-3 definition includes the requirement for a vasopressor infusion and lactate ≥2 mmol/L.
L504: 5 Baseline creatinine refers to closest outpatient creatinine in the last 12 months, or lowest inpatient
L505: creatinine from the current hospitalization if no outpatient value available. Moderate-to-severe liver
L506: disease refers to Child’s B or C cirrhosis and documented portal hypertension; episodes of past upper
L507: gastrointestinal bleeding attributed to portal hypertension; or prior episodes of hepatic
L508: failure/encephalopathy/coma. Chronic lung disease refers to chronic restrictive, obstructive, or vascular
L509: disease resulting in severe exercise restriction, i.e., unable to climb stairs or perform household duties;
L510: or documented chronic hypoxia, hypercapnia, secondary polycythemia, severe pulmonary hypertension
L511: (>40 mmHg), or respiratory dependency. Immunosuppression refers to malignancy requiring
L512: chemotherapy treatment in last 3 months; or neutropenia (absolute neutrophil count <0.5 x 10 [9] /L); or
L513: receiving chronic immunosuppressive medications (azathioprime, cyclosporine, cyclophosphamde,
L514: tacrolimus, methotrexate, mycophenolate, anti-TNF agents, interleukin-2 agents) or transplantation
L515: (including stem cell) at any time; or HIV positive.
L516: 6 Systemic (oral or IV) corticosteroids in the intensive care unit before randomization.
L517: 7 Calculated according to the method in NEJM 2017; 377: 419–430.
